---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — JAC's Class"
  description="JAC's Class is built by a British teacher in France. Free interactive English games for the classroom — no login, no paywall."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>About JAC's Class</h1>

      <p>
        JAC's Class is a small, free library of interactive games for English-language teachers.
        Hangman, Jeopardy, Taboo, Codenames, Blockbusters — the classics, built to play in a real classroom on a real projector,
        without logins, accounts, or paywalls.
      </p>

      <h2>Built by a teacher, in a classroom</h2>
      <p>
        I'm JAC — a British teacher based in France. Every game on this site started life as something I needed for my own lessons,
        either with adult learners on technical English programmes or with younger learners working through the CEFR levels.
        If a game is here, it's because I've used it with a real class.
      </p>

      <h2>How games are organised</h2>
      <p>
        Each game has a CEFR level (A1 to C1), a topic, an estimated duration, and a game type.
        You can browse by any of these on the <a href="/games">games page</a>, or jump straight to a level — for example
        <a href="/level/B1">B1 Intermediate</a> — or a game type like <a href="/type/Taboo">Taboo</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Free, and staying that way</h2>
      <p>
        The games will always be free to play directly on this site. The site itself is supported by light display advertising
        once enough teachers are using it — that's how I keep it going without putting anything behind a paywall.
        If you find these useful, the best thing you can do is share them with another teacher.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Suggestions, corrections, requests for a specific topic or level — all very welcome.
        Email <a href="mailto:hello@jaceslclass.com">hello@jaceslclass.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
